From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 20:14:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/25] sync: add degradable query backpressure

Add a closed connection-level degradable root-query declaration and lifecycle capability. Preserve the legacy Connect and one-shot pressure shapes when omitted, reject malformed bounded fields and duplicate negotiation, and keep the feature inert when its optional leader cap is unset.

Gate only degradable root cache-miss leaders before cache-work publication. Normal and dependency queries, mutations, actions, descendants, and undeclared connections retain normal admission.

On admission deferral, retain the exact backend-owned query subset and retry only that subset at the current sync timestamp. Keep successful subscriptions mounted, give ordinary updates precedence, keep feature-unavailable timing independent, and expose active, updated, and cleared pressure epochs with one deduplicated client-triggered retry per epoch.

Expose closed bounded admission, ownership, lifecycle, retry, and pressure metrics. Cover protocol compatibility, timer races, removal and unchanged recovery, reconnect and shutdown, chunking, permit accounting, and companion convex-js and frontend contracts in the maintained patch documentation.
